From c3168e207a020e03d0e71d3d43e19353d7a87186 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <jufangjian@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:21:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] run dispose on the rollout owner loop with
 bounded deadlines

Production rollout functions run on the shared background AsyncLoopThread
(call_rollout_function -> async_utils.run), so awaiting aclose()/rh2 close
from the Ray actor loop is a foreign-loop await that may never wake. New
miles/utils/rh2_shutdown.py posts the whole close sequence (aclose ->
first cause -> rh2 close_bringup_service) back onto the owner loop via
run_coroutine_threadsafe and the actor awaits the wrapped future with a
total timeout (default 900s, args.rh2_dispose_timeout_sec /
RH2_MILES_DISPOSE_TIMEOUT_SEC). FullyAsyncRolloutFn.aclose() gains a
shutdown deadline (default 60s, args.rh2_shutdown_deadline_sec /
RH2_MILES_SHUTDOWN_DEADLINE_SEC) for cancelling worker and active groups,
records unfinished counts, and closes the buffer in finally so blocked
put/get waiters always wake. train_async wraps everything from
create_rollout_manager onward in try/finally and passes a serialisable
driver_cause to dispose; a worker fatal keeps precedence as first cause.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
